Answer:
- A government agency may collect or use personal data without an individual's consent only in the cases listed under section 5 of the document, which include:
  - i. such collection or use is for any of the purposes in Section 4 of the Public Sector (Governance) Act and to the extent required by any Ministerial Direction issued under the Act, and the agency is collecting or using the personal data is a Singapore public sector agency as defined in Section 2 of the Act;
  - ii. such collection or use is authorised by any other law or required by order of court;
  - iii. such collection or use is necessary in the public interest (including without limitation national interest);
  - iv. such disclosure is permitted without consent by the exclusions in Annex A or Part 2 of Annex B and complies with all applicable legal obligations; or
  - v. the individual that the personal data relates to, gives, or is deemed to give, his consent to the collection or use (as applicable) of his personal data by the agency for the purposes set out in paragraph 21. [Document: government-personal-data-protection-policies-jul21.pdf, Page 11]
